<Doc title="Docs" description="SEGAN documentation: the agent workflow, the full notation reference and the changelog.">
  <h1>SEGAN docs</h1>
  <p>
    These pages are generated from the files that ship with SEGAN, so they always match the release.
    The same text is what your agent reads: the skill installs it into your repo, and the MCP server
    serves it as <code>segan://workflow</code> and <code>segan://reference</code>.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={asset("docs/workflow/")}>Workflow</a>: how an agent sets up a game's audio, reads listen sheets, makes SFX and songs, and changes the sound over time.</li>
    <li><a href={asset("docs/reference/")}>Notation reference</a>: kits, SFX, songs, <code>segan.toml</code>, commands, lint rules, build output, Godot.</li>
    <li><a href={asset("docs/changelog/")}>Changelog</a>: every release, and what forces a version bump.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Five-minute start</h2>
  <pre><code>pip install "git+https://github.com/lukasgolino/segan.git@v0.1.0"
segan init audio --style chiptune   # segan.toml, BRIEF.md, SOUND.md, kits/chip.kit.yaml
cd audio
segan kit show                      # every instrument: previews/kits/chip.listen.png + WAVs
segan new sfx coin --preset coin --description "bright two-note pickup"
segan new song theme --key "A minor" --tempo 120 --description "exploration loop"
segan lint && segan preview coin theme
segan build                         # WAVs + manifest.json (+ Godot resources)</code></pre>
  <h2>Sister library</h2>
  <p><a href="https://pagan.top/">PAGAN</a> does the same for pixel art: sprites, tiles and 3D-rendered headings as text.</p>
  <p><a href="https://lukasgolino.com/kiln-website/">KILN</a> does it for smooth, stylised 3D: models written as shapes that blend like clay, built into glTF and Godot scenes.</p>
</Doc>
